    226  0758							; --------------------------------------------------------- {5}
    227  0758							; The seam: player 1 moves to the guard of the band {5}
    228  0758							; below. The count zcnt reaches 0 in line B1 of the course {5}
    229  0758							; c of the seam (main.asm: p1_bands); from there to the end {5}
    230  0758							; of line A0 of course c + 1 player 1 draws nothing, and {5}
    231  0758							; these lines do in turn what the kernel needs to move it: {5}
    232  0758							;   B1  (the rest)  prepares A2 as B1 does {5}
    233  0758							;   A2  reads PF1 and PF2 of course c + 1, prepares B2, {5}
    234  0758							;	 REFP1 of the guard below {5}
    235  0758							;   B2  prepares A3 and the figure of Sir Roderick for B3 {5}
    236  0758							;   A3  waits zcoarse x 5 cycles, then RESP1: the coarse {5}
    237  0758							;	 column (15 pixels per 5 cycles; RESP1 writes a cycle {5}
    238  0758							;	 after place's, so the count and the fine move are {5}
    239  0758							;	 place's for the column - 3) {5}
    240  0758							;   B3  HMOVE first: the fine move (HMP1, written in the HUD {5}
    241  0758							;	 after HMCLR, SC_HM); its comb blanks pixels 0-7 of {5}
    242  0758							;	 this line, which is the mortar of block column 0 {5}
    243  0758							;	 (never in the courses of the openings); the pointer {5}
    244  0758							;	 of the graphics of the guard below; PF2 of course {5}
    245  0758							;	 c + 1 (in its window, after the right half) {5}
    246  0758							;   A0  as A0, and the pointer of the colours {5}
    247  0758							; then back to the end of A0, and the kernel goes on with {5}
    248  0758							; the guard below. Sir Roderick is drawn in every line. {5}
